## ✅ Fixed Top Bar Title Display

### **What Changed:**
- **Before**: Top bar showed "CoreDroid" as main title and screen name as subtitle
- **After**: Top bar shows **only the current screen title** as the main title

### **Current Behavior:**
The top bar now dynamically displays:

- **"Overview"** when on Overview screen 
- **"Hardware"** when on Hardware screen
- **"System"** when on System screen 
- **"Network"** when on Network screen
- **"Network Monitoring"** when on Network Monitoring screen
- **"Sensors"** when on Sensors screen
- **"Sensor Details"** when viewing sensor details

### **UI Structure Now:**
```
 Top Bar: [Current Screen Title Only]
 Content: [Screen Content]
 Bottom: [Icon-only navigation] (hidden on detail screens)
```

### **Benefits:**
1. **Cleaner Look** - No redundant "CoreDroid" text
2. **Clear Navigation** - Users always know which screen they're on
3. **Better Space Usage** - More room for the actual screen title
4. **Consistent Experience** - Same pattern across all screens

The app now has a much cleaner and more focused top bar that shows exactly what screen the user is currently viewing, without any redundant branding text!"}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"
