 .padding(vertical = 2.dp),
 colors = CardDefaults.cardColors(
 containerColor = MaterialTheme.colorScheme.surfaceVariant
 ),
 shape = RoundedCornerShape(8.dp),
 elevation = CardDefaults.cardElevation(defaultElevation = 2.dp)
 ) {
 Row(
 modifier = Modifier.padding(vertical = 10.dp, horizontal = 10.dp),
 verticalAlignment = Alignment.CenterVertically
 ) {
 Text(
 text = timeFormat.format(Date(event.timestamp)),
 style = MaterialTheme.typography.labelMedium,
 color = MaterialTheme.colorScheme.primary,
 fontWeight = FontWeight.Medium,
 modifier = Modifier.width(70.dp)
 )
 Spacer(Modifier.width(8.dp))
 Text(
 text = event.type,
 modifier = Modifier.width(72.dp),
 color = when (event.type) {
 "WIFI" -> CoreDroidColors.Success
 "MOBILE" -> CoreDroidColors.Warning
 "STATUS" -> CoreDroidColors.Primary
 "SIGNAL" -> CoreDroidColors.Info
 "ERROR" -> CoreDroidColors.Error
 else -> MaterialTheme.colorScheme.onSurface
 },
 fontWeight = FontWeight.Bold
 )
 Spacer(Modifier.width(8.dp))
 Text(
 text = event.description,
 style = MaterialTheme.typography.bodySmall,
 color = MaterialTheme.colorScheme.onSurfaceVariant,
 modifier = Modifier.weight(1f)
 )
 }
 }
}
```

---

## **Design Summary**
- **TopBar**: Modern, color-coordinated, unified with the app’s palette.
- **Banner**: Card highlighting “LIVE”/“OFF” state.
- **Network Cards**: Stacked, large, easy to scan.
- **Events**: Scrollable, each in a subtle card with colored type.
- **Button**: Large and sticky at bottom for “Stop Monitoring”.

---

### Now your monitoring UI will:
- Be much easier to scan at a glance.
- Look clean and modern.
- Make “Stop Monitoring” always discoverable.
- Visually highlight state and problems.
- Scale well to all phone sizes and for long event feeds.

You can further tune iconography, animation, or transitions, but this will give you a professional, up-to-date foundation!"}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"
